repository-code: "https://github.com/MyeongHaHwang/DER-SafeAgent"
abstract: >
  DER-SafeAgent is a runtime-assurance architecture in which an untrusted
  LLM advisory component (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct or Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct with
  locally served QLoRA adapters; vendor APIs deliberately excluded) is
  bounded by deterministic mechanisms — an observable-evidence gate, a
  safety-projection shield over a fixed mitigation registry, mandatory
  escalation of irreversible actions, and a hash-chained audit record — that
  translate intrusion-detection alerts into bounded, auditable cyber-physical
  mitigation actions for DER-rich distribution networks. Deterministic
  runtime-assurance mechanisms provide the containment guarantees; the LLM is
  treated as an untrusted advisory component. This repository ships the
  implementation, frozen experiment protocols, synthetic datasets, canonical
  result files, and the scripts that regenerate the manuscript's tables and
  figures.
keywords:
  - distributed energy resources
  - critical energy infrastructure
  - cyber-physical security
  - operational technology
  - runtime assurance
  - large language model agents
  - incident response
license: Apache-2.0
notes: >
  Repository directories and Python package names retain the legacy system
  name DER-SecAgent to preserve recorded configuration hashes.
